+# Tool Input Validation
+
+| Field  | Value                |
+| ------ | -------------------- |
+| Issue  | re-cinq/HALEngine#37 |
+| Status | In Progress          |
+
+`ToolRegistry.execute` validates caller-supplied `input` against the resolved tool definition's `inputSchema` before invoking the tool's executor. When validation fails, `execute` returns a `ToolResponse` whose `result` describes the failing property paths and constraints without ever invoking the executor or throwing an exception, allowing the model to correct its call on the next tool round within `maxToolRounds`. An unknown tool name continues to throw `Unknown tool: <name>`.
+
+## Schema Compilation and Registration
+
+- `ToolRegistry.register` compiles a static tool definition's `inputSchema` at registration time and throws an error naming the tool if the schema cannot be compiled ([validated by: rejects an uncompilable schema at registration time and names the tool](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L83)).
+- A static tool's schema is compiled once at registration rather than recompiled on every `execute` call.
+- A function-valued `ToolDefinitionSource` resolves per call and validates `input` against the schema returned for that call, caching compiled validators by schema object reference ([validated by: validates a function-valued tool definition against the schema current at each call](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L98)).
+
+## Validation and Rejection Contract
+
+- When `input` fails the resolved `inputSchema` (such as a missing `required` property, a wrong declared type, or a value outside an `enum`), `ToolRegistry.execute` returns a `ToolResponse` naming the failing property path and constraint without invoking the executor ([validated by: returns a ToolResponse naming the missing required property and never calls the executor](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L13)).
+- Validation enforces `required`, declared types, and `enum` only; it does not inject `additionalProperties: false`, coerce types, or apply defaults, so valid input carrying unlisted extra properties is passed to the executor unchanged.
+- Rejection messages and log lines name the failing property path and expected constraint, and never include the offending property value ([validated by: rejects a wrong-typed field naming the property and expected type without leaking the offending value into the result or logs](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L40)).
+- Calling `ToolRegistry.execute` with an unregistered tool name still throws `Unknown tool: <name>`.
+
+## Orchestrator Tool Loop Recovery
+
+- Because a schema rejection returns a `ToolResponse` rather than throwing, `ChatOrchestrator` feeds the rejection `result` back to the provider as a `tool_result` message so the model can issue a corrected tool call on the next round and resolve `processMessage` ([validated by: feeds a schema rejection back to the provider as a tool_result and resolves after a corrected retry](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L134)).
